Alyssa (Docs): Quick sync: I'm about to open PR #4123 with embed-sharding examples for lyra-embed-8b, but I hit a 404 from a stale link in the model card. Can someone eyeball before I push?

Mike (ML): Which link? I can check.

Alyssa (Docs): It points to /docs/embeddings/sharding (404). New canonical guide lives at /guides/embeddings/sharding.

Mike (ML): Got it. We should also clarify sequence limits for the quantized variant. Current internal tests show odd truncation behavior past 8192 tokens. Recommend note: "sequence_limit: 8192 — quantized-8bit will best-effort truncate and may degrade embedding quality near the cutoff."

Sophia (SDK): I noticed the example uses the legacy .embed() shape. We now use the embeddings.create API. Draft snippet: ```js
// Node SDK - embeddings
const res = await client.embeddings.create({
  model: 'lyra-embed-8b',
  input: ['Hello world', 'Another text']
});
```
I'll push that small change to the PR.

Alyssa (Docs): Please include a short client-side sharding pattern and a note saying we do not recommend using internal headers like X-Embed-Shard in hosted.

Samir (Eng): Agree. Add deterministic client slicing example (hash-bucket) instead of suggesting internal headers. Quick pseudocode I recommend: ```js
function shardInputs(inputs, shardCount) {
  const shards = Array.from({length: shardCount}, () => []);
  inputs.forEach((txt) => {
    const bucket = stableHash(txt) % shardCount;
    shards[bucket].push(txt);
  });
  return shards;
}
// then call embeddings.create per shard
```
Mention using a stable hash lib.

DocsBot: PR #4123 CI report: embed smoke tests failing for single-input sequences > 8192 tokens on lyra-embed-8b quantized-8bit. @Mike to confirm recommended doc language.

Mike (ML): Confirmed. Behavior: quantized-8bit models will drop tail tokens beyond 8192 and may return lower-quality vectors. Add explicit limit and a short quality caveat.

Eva (PM): Can we add a one-liner about tradeoffs? Teams often shard and think throughput is always better. Suggest: "Sharding can increase throughput but adds per-shard overhead; prefer batching when latency is critical."

Sophia (SDK): I'll add a tip in the snippet: "Tip: batch shards to improve throughput; keep per-shard payloads < ~400KB to avoid client timeouts" and show how to parallelize requests with Promise.all.

Alyssa (Docs): Also, the catalog index links /models/lyra (old slug) — can infra add a redirect to /catalog/models/lyra-embed-8b? Otherwise a bunch of inbound links will 404. @Samir

Samir (Eng): Filed infra-redirects#27. I'll deploy a 301 redirect and update the canonical slug. ETA ~25 minutes. Will post when live.

Alyssa (Docs): Great. Once redirect is live I'll update the model card and merge.

Samir (Eng): Redirect is deployed and tested (301 works).

Alyssa (Docs): CI is green after Sophia's SDK tweak, and I've updated the model card to include the sequence_limit note and the sharding guidance. Merged PR #4123. Closing this thread — thanks! :tada:

Sophia (SDK): Nice work. I'll follow up with a tiny SDK release note mentioning the embeddings API snippet change.

Mike (ML): Thanks all. Logged a follow-up to monitor embedding quality near the 8k boundary.

Eva (PM): Heads-up to the support team about the limit so they can triage questions.

Alyssa (Docs): Added a brief blurb to the release notes and pinged support. Closing.
